FFmpeg also includes ffmpeg-dovi-padding.patch (LGPL-2.1+): ignore NAL trailing_zero_8bits
before Dolby RPU extension detection. This avoids interpreting zero padding as DM v2 metadata;
the unmodified picture/RPU content and CRC checks remain intact. Patch shipped with the framework.

FFmpeg includes ffmpeg-mov-trun-cts.patch (LGPL-2.1+): preserve signed version-1
composition offsets while deriving fragment decode timestamps from MFRA presentation times.
Without the sign extension, a negative offset became approximately 2^32 ticks, corrupting
later B-frame segment timestamps. The patch is shipped with the framework for rebuilding/relinking.

FFmpeg includes ffmpeg-mkv-skip-attachments.patch (LGPL-2.1+): the Matroska demuxer skips
attached file data (fonts, cover images) instead of reading it. AirPlay never uses attachments,
and over a network link they were read in full before the first picture. The patch is shipped
with the framework for rebuilding/relinking.
